   "vocabulary": {
    "Distributed per full headright; the Osage Minerals Council prints a divisor of 2228.97393 headrights and rounds the rate back to the nearest $5. THE DIVISOR IS NOT APPLIED HERE - multiplying this rate by it would manufacture an aggregate.": 482,
    "STATUTORY SPLIT FOR NEW WELLS ONLY: trust lands 80% tribe / 20% state; non-trust (fee) lands 20% tribe / 80% state. THIS RATIO MUST NOT BE APPLIED TO THE SERIES. It governs only wells on which drilling first commenced after 2019-06-30; wells spudded earlier stay on the prior split for the life of the well, so every monthly distribution after this date is a BLEND of two regimes weighted by the spud-date mix of producing wells. The published distribution does not decompose by well vintage, and Cedar Press does not model the mix.": 232,
    "ANCSA Section 7(i): 70% of net revenues from timber resources and the subsurface estate is divided among all 12 Alaska-based regional corporations in proportion to original enrollment. ANCSA Section 7(j): not less than 50% of what a regional corporation receives under 7(i) must be redistributed to village corporations and at-large shareholders in its region. THIS FORMULA MUST NOT BE APPLIED TO ANY ROW - the shares are governed by the 1982 Section 7(i) Settlement Agreement and by allowable deductions and cost carryforwards that no report in this source system quantifies.": 185,
    "Trust lands: 50% tribe / 50% state. Non-trust (fee) lands: 50% tribe / 50% state. MATCHED ON PAYMENT DATE, which lags the taxable event, so payments near a boundary may be governed by the adjacent period.": 144,
    "Trust lands: 50% tribe / 50% state. Non-trust (fee) lands: 20% tribe / 80% state. MATCHED ON PAYMENT DATE, which lags the taxable event, so payments near a boundary may be governed by the adjacent period.": 116,
    "SMCRA 30 U.S.C. 1232: 50% of reclamation fees collected in the state or tribal area. THE THREE TRIBAL PROGRAMMES ARE CERTIFIED, so the fee-based share is replaced by an equivalent Certified In Lieu payment. The formula is not applied here and must not be used to derive a collection figure.": 76,
    "Utah Code 59-5-116 (deposits) and 63N-24-601..606 (fund)": 60,
    "Utah Code 59-5-119 (deposits) and 63N-24-701..706 (fund)": 58,
    "Fort Peck agreement sec. VIII: the Tribes receive 50% of the total tax on NEW oil and NEW natural gas production on the Reservation, paid quarterly (sec. VII.B). 'New' means wells on which drilling commenced on or after the effective date; existing production is unaffected.": 49,
    "Total Revenue reproduces the published per-headright rate WITHOUT subtracting the Oklahoma gross production tax, so this vintage reports revenue NET of that tax.": 44,
    "Distributed per full headright; the Osage Minerals Council prints a divisor of 2228.97393 headrights. THE DIVISOR IS NOT APPLIED HERE - multiplying this rate by it would manufacture an aggregate, and the modern divisor is in any case not the 1880 one.": 26,
    "Total Revenue reproduces the published per-headright rate only AFTER subtracting the Oklahoma gross production tax, so this vintage reports revenue GROSS of that tax. NOT COMPARABLE with the pre-2018 vintage without adjustment.": 16,
    "IIJA sec. 40701 apportions by historic coal production tonnage. The tonnage is printed but the apportionment is NOT recomputed here.": 15,
